WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.870
A lot of people look at Black Christmas and
find it scary because of how crazy and unpredictable

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:06.759
the killer, Billy, seems to be.

00:00:06.759 --> 00:00:11.099
I have to disagree though, I have a theory
about the psychological motivation behind

00:00:11.099 --> 00:00:12.099
his crimes.

00:00:12.099 --> 00:00:16.620
Stick around to the end of this video if you
want to hear it.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:19.240
[intro]

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:22.862
Black Christmas doesn't get enough credit
for being the trend setter that it was.

00:00:22.862 --> 00:00:26.980
It was a holiday themed horror film, and it
opens with a point-of-view shot of the killer

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:28.800
looking through the house's windows.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:32.970
John Carpenter would borrow this technique
for Halloween four years later, and Black

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:37.290
Christmas connected us to some creepy phone
calls decades before Scream.

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:41.070
We see in the beginning of the film that the
attic windows are dark, telling us that this

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:45.030
is the first time Billy has targeted this
house, which does play into my theory that

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:46.600
I'll touch on later.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:49.550
However, this isn't the first time they've
received a call from him.

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:54.280
"Hey quiet, it's him again!

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:56.580
The moaner!"

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:04.820
So they have dealt with Billy as a caller
in the past.

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:08.980
"I'm going to kill you."

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:15.850
We see that the police station is located
at the intersection of Main Street and Swanwick

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:18.950
Avenue, and that places this in Toronto, Canada.

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:21.040
It still looks relatively the same today.

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:23.340
The cop cars are labeled "Bedford Police".

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:27.130
There are a couple of Bedfords in Canada but
none that are near Toronto, so I'm guessing

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:31.950
that Bedford is a fictional town and a slight
nod to the town Bedford Falls from one of

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:36.119
the most classic Christmas movies out there,
It's A Wonderful Life.

00:01:36.119 --> 00:01:42.420
Did anyone notice Mrs. Mac brushes her teeth
even though she has false teeth in the cabinet?

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:48.009
However, despite supposedly having false teeth,
they still look horrible, and as if that wasn't

00:01:48.009 --> 00:01:52.860
enough, she swishes her mouth with alcohol,
and not just any alcohol, but alcohol she

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:54.600
fished out of the toilet tank.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:58.780
If you ask me, that's a lot worse than anything
the killer does in this movie.

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:02.690
The first kill of the movie is Clare, who
is suffocated in her room.

00:02:02.690 --> 00:02:06.119
It's not shown how Billy gets her body up
the ladder to the attic, but there is a clue

00:02:06.119 --> 00:02:10.420
in the second kill, where he impales Mrs.
Mac with this hook and uses the pulley to

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:11.920
reel her straight up.

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:15.720
After this, he goes on a rampage and knocks
over all of the things, while yelling at the

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:17.000
top of his lungs.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:21.850
Later on after Jess has a minor scare downstairs,
Peter comes down and asks what all the yelling

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:22.850
was about.

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:25.290
"You scared the hell out of me too.

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:27.400
What was all the yelling about?"

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:31.790
It wasn't until I watched it for a second
time that I realized Jess wasn't making all

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:36.990
that much noise, and Peter was probably referring
to Billy's yelling, he just didn't know it.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.870
Kind of creepy if you think about it.

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:42.450
After the cops start to connect the occurrences
of Clare going missing with the obscene phone

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:46.319
calls received at the sorority house, they
come by to tap the phones, so that they can

00:02:46.319 --> 00:02:48.310
try to find out where the calls are coming
from.

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:52.489
We already know about two of the phones, the
one in the living and the one in the hall,

00:02:52.489 --> 00:02:55.480
because Barb takes a call on the hall phone
because of all the noise around the living

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:57.709
room phone in the opening holiday party scene.

00:02:57.709 --> 00:03:00.400
What we don't know is that there's another
phone in the house.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.360
"Are there any other phones in the house?"

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:03.360
"Yes, the housemother has..."

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:06.040
"Yes, but it's another number and there haven't
been any calls."

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:09.820
This explains how Billy is able to make the
calls from within the house.

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:12.000
"Your phone's ringing."

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.080
"Oh, yes.

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:16.370
Excuse me.

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:17.370
Goodnight."

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:18.910
"Certainly, goodnight."

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:23.710
Later in the film, the soundtrack shifts with
the subject matter, going from jolly Christmas

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:24.940
to a much darker tone.

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:29.500
I guess Bob Clark really liked the sound of
Peter smashing the piano after his recital,

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:33.100
because it can be heard several times throughout
the second half of the movie.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:48.660
*smashed piano sound*

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:50.480
"Claude are you up here?"

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:57.080
"Don't you tell what we did Agnes."

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:02.480
*screaming*

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:11.600
I've seen plenty of reviewers praise Black
Christmas for it's ambiguous villain and lack

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:16.220
of a real conclusion leaving them chilled
and uneasy and for this reason, I have to

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:21.169
include my theory about the reason for Billy's
crime spree in my Things You Missed.

00:04:21.169 --> 00:04:23.820
Take this review on Culture Crypt as an example.

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:28.539
"Besides, how could Billy’s origin and the
killer’s motivations ever be more satisfying

00:04:28.539 --> 00:04:32.900
than the disturbing nonsense of frightening
phone calls and the threat of unknown deaths

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:35.210
occurring behind closed doors?"

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:40.340
Well, maybe the happenings of Black Christmas
aren't as nonsensical as they appear.

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:43.300
The first scene Billy is in is the opening
scene.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:47.189
As I mentioned before, we see from his point
of view as he skulks around the house and

00:04:47.189 --> 00:04:48.629
looks through windows.

00:04:48.629 --> 00:04:53.060
Staring through the windows of a sorority
house screams Peeping Tom, and we are quickly

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:58.210
given more evidence that the crimes are sensually
motivated during Billy's first phone call,

00:04:58.210 --> 00:05:02.639
where he can be heard breathing, moaning and
choking before getting into laughter and snorting

00:05:02.639 --> 00:05:03.639
like a pig.

00:05:03.639 --> 00:05:08.139
Pig is often the word used to describe those
without restraint when it comes to sensual

00:05:08.139 --> 00:05:09.389
subject matters.

00:05:09.389 --> 00:05:12.180
From there, the language gets much more explicit.

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:16.270
It's no coincidence that he targets a house
of 10 women, nine of whom are college students

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:20.529
who decorate their walls with dirty posters
and give out fake phone numbers containing

00:05:20.529 --> 00:05:24.860
"the newest exchanges", or in other words,
terms that are not safe for work.

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:30.139
You'll also notice that all of Billy's victims
are female, with the exception of one and

00:05:30.139 --> 00:05:31.189
there's a reason for it.

00:05:31.189 --> 00:05:37.259
They include Clare, Mrs. Mac, Barb who's taken
out in a very phallic manner, and Phyl who

00:05:37.259 --> 00:05:38.280
dies offscreen.

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:42.149
There's also mention of something happening
to a girl in town a couple weeks ago -- could

00:05:42.149 --> 00:05:46.979
be related and also the high school girl found
in the park -- again, may or may not be related.

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:51.460
The only male death is Officer Jennings, which
was only necessary for Billy because he was

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:53.180
interfering with him getting to Jess.

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:57.169
Keep in mind there are men staying in the
house throughout the movie, but none of them

00:05:57.169 --> 00:05:58.169
are attacked.

00:05:58.169 --> 00:06:01.979
Jess's boyfriend Peter also becomes a victim,
but Billy isn't the one responsible.

00:06:01.979 --> 00:06:06.009
"It's hard to believe Jess would kill anybody,
much less Peter."

00:06:06.009 --> 00:06:10.279
However, there's more to this than Billy just
being some kind of vengeful incel who decided

00:06:10.279 --> 00:06:12.139
to ruin Christmas.

00:06:12.139 --> 00:06:13.139
Like the Grinch.

00:06:13.139 --> 00:06:16.159
If you pay attention to Billy's ramblings,
you'll notice he's constantly referencing

00:06:16.159 --> 00:06:17.759
someone named Agnes.

00:06:17.759 --> 00:06:22.349
He holds entire conversations in his head
with Agnes in which he plays both parts.

00:06:22.349 --> 00:06:26.309
*Crying*
"No Billy, no!"

00:06:26.309 --> 00:06:28.289
"The knife!"

00:06:28.289 --> 00:06:30.270
"No Billy!

00:06:30.270 --> 00:06:32.249
No Billy.

00:06:32.249 --> 00:06:34.229
No Billy!"

00:06:34.229 --> 00:06:35.229
*Crying*

00:06:35.229 --> 00:06:41.120
The 2006 film has a character named Agnes
who is Billy's sister, but there's no confirmation

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:42.229
of that in the original.

00:06:42.229 --> 00:06:46.509
However, we can infer that Agnes is Billy's
sister based on this scene later in the movie

00:06:46.509 --> 00:06:49.759
where he's brought his mother into the fold
as one of the characters.

00:06:49.759 --> 00:06:50.849
"Mommy..."

00:06:50.849 --> 00:06:53.020
"Come here!"

00:06:53.020 --> 00:06:54.110
"Mommy!"

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:55.280
"Where's Agnes?"

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:59.520
*Crazy laughter*
"Agnes!"

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:01.760
*Screaming and Choking*
"See Mommy?

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:03.120
There's the baby.

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:05.680
Baby alright Mommy."

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:09.800
He seems to be crying to his mother as she
attacks him, demanding to know where Agnes

00:07:09.819 --> 00:07:10.889
is at.

00:07:10.889 --> 00:07:14.159
From that, I would conclude Agnes most likely
is his sister.

00:07:14.159 --> 00:07:18.789
In fact, Billy kind of illustrates this fact
by using Clare's corpse to create his mother

00:07:18.789 --> 00:07:23.099
figure by putting her on the rocking chair
with a baby doll and using his hand to rock

00:07:23.099 --> 00:07:24.289
the chair for her.

00:07:24.289 --> 00:07:28.770
Using all the clues I've presented, I'll let
you come to your own conclusion about what

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:33.229
Billy is referring to when he exclaims, "Don't
tell what we did Agnes."

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:35.520
"Agnes it's me Billy.

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:40.200
It's alright Agnes, it's alright.

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:41.760
Shhh!

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:43.679
Pretty Agnes."

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:48.909
"Don't tell what we did Agnes."

00:07:48.909 --> 00:07:52.289
You may still be wondering, why does all this
happen around Christmas?

00:07:52.289 --> 00:07:54.339
Why has he waited until now to strike.

00:07:54.339 --> 00:07:57.689
I think Christmas is a day that takes us all
back to our childhoods in a way.

00:07:57.689 --> 00:08:01.439
It's the day that kids most look forward to
all year unless you are like me, then you

00:08:01.439 --> 00:08:04.989
look forward to Halloween, but the point is
that you're always reminded of your childhood

00:08:04.989 --> 00:08:05.989
on Christmas.

00:08:05.989 --> 00:08:10.340
In Billy's case, remembering his childhood,
whatever abuse that might have consisted of,

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:14.409
brings up repressed memories and causes him
to revert to a childlike state.

00:08:14.409 --> 00:08:18.830
This is the reason Billy sings the nursery
rhyme Little Baby Bunting after wrapping Clare's

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:21.320
body in plastic.

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:33.440
"Little baby Bunting.

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:36.840
Daddy's gone a hunting.

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:40.200
Gone to fetch a rabbit skin.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:46.200
To wrap his baby Agnes in..."

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:51.160
He also throws what can only be described
as a temper tantrum.

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:58.640
*Screaming*

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:02.670
And I think the phone ringing at the end of
the film tells us all we need to know about

00:09:02.670 --> 00:09:03.670
Jess's fate.

00:09:03.670 --> 00:09:07.310
Let me know your own interpretations of Black
Christmas in the comments, and if you'd like

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:10.730
to see me cover the 2006 version of Black
Christmas as well.

